<p>If KVM guests in <code>virt-manager</code> doesn't work, tail the journal for <code>libvirtd</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>root@mithrandir ~ # journalctl -f -u libvirtd
Aug 08 22:13:02 mithrandir systemd[1]: Started libvirt legacy monolithic daemon.
Aug 08 22:13:54 mithrandir libvirtd[6138]: libvirt version: 12.6.0
Aug 08 22:13:54 mithrandir libvirtd[6138]: hostname: mithrandir, uid: 0
Aug 08 22:13:54 mithrandir libvirtd[6138]: invalid argument: could not find capabilities for arch=x86_64
^OAug 08 22:16:25 mithrandir systemd[1]: libvirtd.service: Deactivated successfully.
</code></pre></div>

<p>I remedied the error above by installing the <code>quemu-desktop</code> package:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code># root@mithrandir ~ # pacman -S qemu-desktop
</code></pre></div>

<p>I then had to re-enable and restart <code>libvirtd</code>:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code># systemctl enable libvirtd
# systemctl restart libvirtd
</code></pre></div>